{"tool_name":"bigstitcher","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"BigStitcher","home":"https://imagej.net/BigStitcher","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Reconstructing high-resolution image datasets of cleared and expanded samples | ImgLib2/BDV implementation of Stitching for large datasets | The BigStitcher is a software package that allows simple and efficient alignment of multi-tile and multi-angle image datasets, for example acquired by lightsheet, widefield or confocal microscopes. The software supports images of almost arbitrary size ranging from very small images up to volumes in the range of many terabytes, which are for example produced when acquiring cleared tissue samples with lightsheet microscopy","addition_date":"2019-11-14T18:14:21Z","last_update_date":"2020-12-05T14:40:37Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:BigStitcher","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Microscope image visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3552"},{"term":"Sequence merging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0232"}]}],"name":"BigStitcher","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-019-0501-0","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019, The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Springer Nature America, Inc.Light-sheet imaging of cleared and expanded samples creates terabyte-sized datasets that consist of many unaligned three-dimensional image tiles, which must be reconstructed before analysis. We developed the BigStitcher software to address this challenge. BigStitcher enables interactive visualization, fast and precise alignment, spatially resolved quality estimation, real-time fusion and deconvolution of dual-illumination, multitile, multiview datasets. The software also compensates for optical effects, thereby improving accuracy and enabling subsequent biological analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Cardona A."},{"name":"Chhetri R.K."},{"name":"Harz H."},{"name":"Horl D."},{"name":"Keller P.J."},{"name":"Leonhardt H."},{"name":"Preibisch S."},{"name":"Preusser F."},{"name":"Randel N."},{"name":"Rojas Rusak F."},{"name":"Tillberg P."},{"name":"Treier M."}],"citationCount":50,"date":"2019-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"BigStitcher: reconstructing high-resolution image datasets of cleared and expanded samples"},"pmid":"31384047"}],"topic":[{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"BigStitcher","home":"https://bio.tools/BigStitcher","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Reconstructing high-resolution image datasets of cleared and expanded samples | ImgLib2/BDV implementation of Stitching for large datasets | The BigStitcher is a software package that allows simple and efficient alignment of multi-tile and multi-angle image datasets, for example acquired by lightsheet, widefield or confocal microscopes. The software supports images of almost arbitrary size ranging from very small images up to volumes in the range of many terabytes, which are for example produced when acquiring cleared tissue samples with lightsheet microscopy","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:bigstitcher/undefined/imagej.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":183,"citations":[{"count":6,"year":"2019"},{"count":18,"year":"2026"},{"count":19,"year":"2020"},{"count":22,"year":"2023"},{"count":24,"year":"2024"},{"count":26,"year":"2022"},{"count":30,"year":"2021"},{"count":38,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41592-019-0501-0","pmid":"31384047","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"BigStitcher: reconstructing high-resolution image datasets of cleared and expanded samples.","year":2019}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/bigstitcher"},{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/bigstitcher/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bigstitcher","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/bigstitcher"},{"status":301,"url":"https://imagej.net/plugins/bigstitcher/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>The BigStitcher is a software package that allows simple and efficient alignment of multi-tile and multi-angle image datasets, for example acquired by lightsheet, widefield or confocal microscopes. The software supports images of almost arbitrary size ranging from very small images up to volumes in the range of many terabytes, which are for example produced when acquiring cleared tissue samples with lightsheet microscopy.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>The BigStitcher is a software package that allows simple and efficient alignment of multi-tile and multi-angle image datasets, for example acquired by lightsheet, widefield or confocal microscopes. The software supports images of almost arbitrary size ranging from very small images up to volumes in the range of many terabytes, which are for example produced when acquiring cleared tissue samples with lightsheet microscopy.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2025-10-27T07:39:33+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d